# `direnv allow` once, and the dev shell is on whenever you are in this
# directory — same shell `bin/*` re-enter by themselves, so this is convenience,
# not a requirement.
#
# nix-direnv is what makes it bearable: plain `use flake` re-evaluates the flake
# on every cd, which is seconds each time, and holds no GC root, so the next
# `nix store gc` throws the Android SDK away. It caches the shell instead, and
# re-evaluates only when flake.nix or flake.lock changes. Sourced from the URL
# so a fresh checkout needs nothing installed beyond nix and direnv; if you
# already have nix-direnv in ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc, that one wins and this
# is skipped.
if ! has nix_direnv_version || ! nix_direnv_version 3.2.0; then
  source_url "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nix-community/nix-direnv/3.2.0/direnvrc" "sha256-hW6NC1JHue3IjZN3uDM6l6I2PMaauqd2D7hXYJ1Zfr4="
fi

use flake
